owerful spirits? Do as thy wish.<br /> <br /> It isn't particularly rare for those things to happen, so nothing breaks if you decide an Incarna is holding court in New York.<br /> <br /> 4. Likewise, huge areas almost empty of active spirits aren't particularly rare. Completely empty, or a place where even dormant spirits are few, are weird. But you're ok with a Penumbra that's so empty you only find a stray Gaffling every now and then in most blocks.<br /> <br /> 5. Astral Penumbra is even more variable. You don't have to feel a need to put any spirit in the city at all if you don't want, because they have more access to a Realm called the Vulgate, so its even easier to justify them not sticking around.<br /> <br /> Yet for the same reason they have a more direct contact with Earth from there, so it isn't abnormal to have a lot of spirits in a place you think should have.<br /> <br /> 6. Ghosts are the slightly more complex point, because they will define a lot of how you want to run themes of death and lingering dead.<br /> <br /> The game has usually assumed they're far more common in the Penumbra than other spirits, sometimes even forming parallel communities with rules and stuff.<br /> <br /> You don't have to do this, it is perfectly fine to decide that most of them go to the actual Underworld, but the default would be a few times more numerous than other spirits if you make those uncommon.<br /> <br /> And if you really want to emphasize that people leave unfinished business and linger around after death more often than not, you can have a city with a Ghost population as big as a 1/10 of the living population. The game won't break.<br /> <br /> 7. You adjust how hard it is to affect a spirit by messing with three things: number of successes, giving them a Counterspell/Resistance roll, or adding Quintessence requirements.<br /> <br /> Number of successes is the simplest path to make it a challenge, but still feasible. The catch for the Mage isn't just that the spirit requires more to affect, but that they can usually react to the Mage during a ritual.<br /> <br /> Counterspell has a number of possible rules and can become quite nasty, because spirits and Night Folk can have pretty high dice pools. I recommend using this only against effects that are useful with only 1 or 2 successes.<br /> <br /> The good thing is that you don't have to be consistent about it with spirits: the ability to resist and to which type of Magic can be a case by case thing.<br /> <br /> Quintessence is useful when you want to emphasize that there's something fundamental about the nature of that spirit, it isn't just a monster, but an aspect of reality.<br /> <br /> And in practical terms to turn any binding ambition into a fetch quest.<br /> <br /> You decide a Resonance and/or Synergy it has to have, a number of points, and let your players figure out how to get it. That way you don't have to make the Magic itself hard, you turn the preparation into a storyline.<br /> <br /> 8. Other than that, just be bold and make decisions. Are there really three Penumbrae or only one? Do Astral spirits, Wild spirits and Ghosts interact? What's the difference between a Vidare and the Penumbra? What exactly is the difference between the Penumbra and the space between it and other Realms?<br /> <br /> The answer to all of those is whatever, the game is obnoxiously vague and inconsistent, partly on purpose.<br /> <br /> Ideally the answer should be &quot;whatever the Mage believes&quot; and the whole thing should change rules based on Paradigm at the same time that its denizens exist independently of Paradigm.<br /> <br /> But since in practice the ideal is hard as fuck to actually play and that's not a rookie difficulty, it is legitimately inconvenient for everyone, just ignore and do your own stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you so much, this helps a lot! My only issue with making a decent spirit population is the &quot;balance&quot; between Spirit and the other spheres; I am afraid &quot;easy&quot; access to spirits and ghosts would escalate the power level of the spere really quickly. <br /> <br /> As a general &quot;feel&quot; I think some gaffling and some ghosts are bound to be in a city penumbra (if only to make Giovanni Clan make sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and more powerful stuff would be story based. I hope tough that going at it like this I don't cause Spirit to be less powerful than the other spheres<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-03T05:59:31-07:00","id":1564505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564502#post1564502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you so much, this helps a lot! My only issue with making a decent spirit population is the &quot;balance&quot; between Spirit and the other spheres; I am afraid &quot;easy&quot; access to spirits and ghosts would escalate the power level of the spere really quickly.<br /> <br /> As a general &quot;feel&quot; I think some gaffling and some ghosts are bound to be in a city penumbra (if only to make Giovanni Clan make sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and more powerful stuff would be story based. I hope tough that going at it like this I don't cause Spirit to be less powerful than the other spheres</div> </div> </div> </div>So, two things:<br /> <br /> 1. The Spirit Sphere isn't especially powerful by how many spirits you populate the setting with. Spirits are characters and creatures first, so the concern should be primarily the setting you want to build. What do you picture that may happen if you overpopulate? Knowing this will make it easier to explain.<br /> <br /> 2. Do not conflate Umbra and Penumbra. Other realities exist, and the powers that deal with spirits also deal with those realities. The Spirit Sphere can reach the deeper Umbrae and visit other Realms. A Mage that wants to meet an Incarna can go where the Incarna is.<br /> <br /> Similarly, when a Necromancy Path or Ritual says it contacts the Underworld, it isn't talking about the Penumbra. It is talking about another Realm that does have a bazillion ghosts.<br /> <br /> Even if you depopulate the Penumbra those characters still have perfectly normal access to doing their thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-04T03:18:01-07:00","id":1564519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564505#post1564505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, two things:<br /> <br /> 1. The Spirit Sphere isn't especially powerful by how many spirits you populate the setting with. Spirits are characters and creatures first, so the concern should be primarily the setting you want to build. What do you picture that may happen if you overpopulate? Knowing this will make it easier to explain.<br /> <br /> 2. Do not conflate Umbra and Penumbra. Other realities exist, and the powers that deal with spirits also deal with those realities. The Spirit Sphere can reach the deeper Umbrae and visit other Realms. A Mage that wants to meet an Incarna can go where the Incarna is.<br /> <br /> Similarly, when a Necromancy Path or Ritual says it contacts the Underworld, it isn't talking about the Penumbra. It is talking about another Realm that does have a bazillion ghosts.<br /> <br /> Even if you depopulate the Penumbra those characters still have perfectly normal access to doing their thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay maybe I am wrong but I was looking at spirit like a toolbox, more tools equals more power but if they can reach any spirit they want it doesnt really matter how much I populate the penumbra. I am getting that with a little more effort a PC can negotiate/force any kind of spirit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-04T13:23:21-07:00","id":1564521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564519#post1564519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay maybe I am wrong but I was looking at spirit like a toolbox, more tools equals more power but if they can reach any spirit they want it doesnt really matter how much I populate the penumbra. I am getting that with a little more effort a PC can negotiate/force any kind of spirit</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing: they're not.<br /> <br /> Players who talk about how strong Spirit is as a means to do anything are not talking the whole story because they're already used to it.<br /> <br /> Spirits are individual creatures with their own ecology and societies, their own interests, and the Sphere of Spirit <i>does not</i> force them into doing much of anything. Period.<br /> <br /> Also they don't literally do whatever. You don't wake the spirit of a bonfire and suddenly have a portable fire spell. The process is more:<br /> <br /> 1. You rouse the spirit of the bonfire.<br /> <br /> 2. The spirit doesn't care about you and will not cooperate just because, you have to negotiate, be nice for a long time, or good old fashioned violence will do the talking.<br /> <br /> 3. Now you have a measure of control over that bonfire. And not enough to stop iqt from going out when fuel runs out.<br /> <br /> 4. A roused spirit has little power, just a modicum of influence over its direct cause. It doesn't even have stats because it's little more than an object with opinions.<br /> <br /> 5. Other spirits simply have their stats. They do what they can do, and since they're not moored to a specific object anymore, their stats are also the end of it.<br /> <br /> Spirit let you interact with spirits. Not even binding (level 4) can force their compliance. A weak Gaffling isn't smart or independent, but it is not dependent <i>on anyone</i>, they're shadows of the consciousness of a greater spirit. This is a description of intelligence and personality, not of ease to command.<br /> <br /> Individually you still have to communicate and negotiate. Or use other Magic in conjunction with Spirit. And if you Bind a spirit into a Fetish against its will, this Fetish will be both hard to use and dangerous to have around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-04T17:43:59-07:00","id":1564522,"title":"","content":"That<br /> <br /> In a sense, it's a very &quot;social&quot; power. It's not all that unlike how you don't need Forces to lit your ciggarrete if you have a friend with a match. It's a Sphere that opens a lot of posibilities, but also requires a lot of interpretation and can get you into no end of trouble.<br /> <br /> Forcing a spirit to comply with magick it's possible (I don't remember the exact Spheres), but it's very much a can of worms of it's own. To put it simply, unless the spirit you're forcing it's somehow ok with what you're trying to do, you've gained an eternal enemy. Gain a lot of these and powerful spirits of the kind nobody can easily deal with may start taking notice.<br /> <br /> Can a Mind Mage control the President of a Superpower, and try to start wars with countries? - RAW, yes. Should a mage do this? - hell no. Not unless you want to see what the Technocracy's migth can do, and that's if they get to you first.<br /> <br /> Note: Ofc, spirits are much more &quot;esoterical&quot; in the way they work than people (because they're a fictional element). We don't know exactly how all of the Umbra works, and neither do Mages. From Wraith you can learn how could Ghosts would respond to mages. But all spirits have their own hierarchies, responsabilities, etc...Have fun thinking how that interacts with the mage's wishes on cases where you think they're using a little too much spiritual help.<br /> <br /> Like: If a Mage it's creating too many fires with the help of spirits that left alone wouldn't do that, a higher envoy of the Elemental Court of Fire could want to have a talk. If the mage wasn't using force, and just persuaded the spirits, the minister doesn't need to be hostile. Could be curious, could want *in* on whatever deal the spirits have, could tax the mage for repeated use of resources that belong to the Court...it depends on how you think the Fire Elemental &quot;gig&quot; works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-04-2026, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-04T19:31:54-07:00","id":1564523,"title":"","content":"How does the spirit world look to the Mage? However their Focus says it should. A Mage's Paradigm is the filter through which they see everything, whether just looking in from the outside or stepping sideways.<br /> <br /> Even different Mage groups who gravitate towards the same Penumbra type (Astral, Wild, Dark) differ in the specifics.<br /> <br /> A Celestial Chorus miracle worker might see the Astral Penumbra as a place of pure white sunrays and lots of lesser angels flying around. Whereas a Virtual Adept who looks at the Astral Penumbra might see flows of digital information and free-floating programs.<br /> <br /> A Verbana witch's vision of the Spirit Wilds might be covered in roots and vines and sylphs. While an Ecstasy Cultist's vision of the Spirit Wilds is a psychedelic 60s drug trip (even when they're not high).<br /> <br /> A Euthanatos necromancer looks at the Dark Penumbra as a place of fog and shadows and flitting phantoms, maybe with a healthy dose of Hindu stylings (or whatever particular brand of death/fate magic they happen to rep, because the Chakravanti is a big tent). Whereas a Hollow One looks at the Dark Penumbra as something out of a Tim Burton film or gothic horror story. And an Etherite scientist looks through their SpectroScope^TM (patent pending) and sees a lot of grainy images, glitches, and suggestive smears or shapes (basically, look at any &quot;ghost hunter&quot; shows).<br /> <br /> If only one PC is doing the bulk of the Spirit work initially, you can fairly easily tailor the aesthetics of the Umbra/Penumbra to suit their Paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-04T22:21:00-07:00","id":1564526,"title":"","content":"A very simplified break down of the Spirit Sphere in clear language would be as follow:<br /> <br /> 1. You can see invisible ghosts and spirits.<br /> <br /> 2. You interact with invisible ghosts and spirits.<br /> - Also minor Gauntlet tricks.<br /> <br /> 3. You can travel to other worlds.<br /> - Also make things somewhat aware.<br /> <br /> 4. You can open inter dimensional portals.<br /> - Also make Fetishes.<br /> <br /> 5. You can empower spirits and make souls.<br /> - Also your own &quot;pocket&quot; dimensions.<br /> <br /> There is more? Yes. But those will cover 98% of any practical uses.<br /> <br /> Levels 1 and 2 only matter to deal with the Penumbra most of the time, so they deal with spirits close to Earth, but not materialized.<br /> <br /> Levels 3 and 4 mostly deal with travel or making magic items, but their magic items give the Mage less control. You can make an item with powers you don't have, but they're full of their own rules and costs to use. So the bigger impact is often the travel.<br /> <br /> Level 5 can make a lot of things, but they're among the hardest feats of Magic in the game and still require other Spheres for details. The main use ends up being give or drain Essence, which is pretty useful, or create weird matter in other realities, kind like Matter 5 but don't work on Earth. The next simplest feat is to create a human soul and it already requires IIRC 15-20 successes and 5-10 Quintessence.<br /> <br /> And do other Magic work in other worlds without Spirit? Yes, pretty much. They can have stranger rules and effects on Magic. And they can be normal. If you are already in the same dimension as a spirit, most of your Magic will work normally most of the time. Spirit gives an edge, but most other Magic should work just fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T07:06:08-07:00","id":1564530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564501#post1564501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think at the start, for simplicity, I will skip Vidare altogheter and maybe narrate some differences based on the PC paradigms. It sounds like a lot of extra effort for not much flavor, the Otherworlds are already flavorful enough right?<br /> <br /> For the ghosts, I have no idea what to do; I would assume that they are visible in the penumbra, otherwise how would you explain Clan Giovanni in VTM?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts have a place. The Shadowlands exist. The question is how they relate to everything else.<br /> <br /> The Shadowlands are a realm that sits alongside the physical. They are separated form the physical by some kind of barrier (The Shroud). They have the same geography as the physical world, only seen through a lens of death and decay.<br /> <br /> The Penumbra is a realm that sits alongside the physical. It is separated from the physical by some kind of barrier (The Gauntlet). It has the same geography as the physical world, and if someone resonates with the Vidare Mortem the Penumbra will depict everything through a lens of death and decay.<br /> <br /> They sound like the same place with the names changed around. If so then mages are visiting the Shadowlands every time they cross the Gauntlet/Shroud and interacting with ghosts is as easy as interacting with any other spirit they happen to find in the Penumbra. On the other hand, Mage often describes them as two different places, and if that is the case, visiting the realms of the dead is much harder than visiting the realms of the spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T07:36:03-07:00","id":1564533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum