e dimension as a spirit, most of your Magic will work normally most of the time. Spirit gives an edge, but most other Magic should work just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really helpful, it put everything into perspective! Spirit doesn't sound so bad to master at all! I like a lot the social aspect of the sphere!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T07:37:29-07:00","id":1564534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564530#post1564530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghosts have a place. The Shadowlands exist. The question is how they relate to everything else.<br /> <br /> The Shadowlands are a realm that sits alongside the physical. They are separated form the physical by some kind of barrier (The Shroud). They have the same geography as the physical world, only seen through a lens of death and decay.<br /> <br /> The Penumbra is a realm that sits alongside the physical. It is separated from the physical by some kind of barrier (The Gauntlet). It has the same geography as the physical world, and if someone resonates with the Vidare Mortem the Penumbra will depict everything through a lens of death and decay.<br /> <br /> They sound like the same place with the names changed around. If so then mages are visiting the Shadowlands every time they cross the Gauntlet/Shroud and interacting with ghosts is as easy as interacting with any other spirit they happen to find in the Penumbra. On the other hand, Mage often describes them as two different places, and if that is the case, visiting the realms of the dead is much harder than visiting the realms of the spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay this confused me a bit, weren't the shadowlands in the low umbra and incredibily hard to visit if you are alive??<br /> <br /> Cosmology is a problem but that I can kinda simplify without much effort!<br /> <br /> Thank you for helping tough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T07:39:27-07:00","id":1564535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564523#post1564523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the spirit world look to the Mage? However their Focus says it should. A Mage's Paradigm is the filter through which they see everything, whether just looking in from the outside or stepping sideways.<br /> <br /> Even different Mage groups who gravitate towards the same Penumbra type (Astral, Wild, Dark) differ in the specifics.<br /> <br /> A Celestial Chorus miracle worker might see the Astral Penumbra as a place of pure white sunrays and lots of lesser angels flying around. Whereas a Virtual Adept who looks at the Astral Penumbra might see flows of digital information and free-floating programs.<br /> <br /> A Verbana witch's vision of the Spirit Wilds might be covered in roots and vines and sylphs. While an Ecstasy Cultist's vision of the Spirit Wilds is a psychedelic 60s drug trip (even when they're not high).<br /> <br /> A Euthanatos necromancer looks at the Dark Penumbra as a place of fog and shadows and flitting phantoms, maybe with a healthy dose of Hindu stylings (or whatever particular brand of death/fate magic they happen to rep, because the Chakravanti is a big tent). Whereas a Hollow One looks at the Dark Penumbra as something out of a Tim Burton film or gothic horror story. And an Etherite scientist looks through their SpectroScope^TM (patent pending) and sees a lot of grainy images, glitches, and suggestive smears or shapes (basically, look at any &quot;ghost hunter&quot; shows).<br /> <br /> If only one PC is doing the bulk of the Spirit work initially, you can fairly easily tailor the aesthetics of the Umbra/Penumbra to suit their Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>(patent pending) made me laugh quite a bit man! I see this point, not sure tough I wanna go that deep, may settle in one slightly different vision but kinda the same for everyone (a second and a third PCs bought spirit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T09:07:10-07:00","id":1564538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564534#post1564534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay this confused me a bit, weren't the shadowlands in the low umbra and incredibily hard to visit if you are alive??<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't alone. Mage is really a mess on this point. In some places it is really clear that the Shadowlands <b>are</b> the Penumbra (as seen through the Vidare Mortem) and even goes so far as to say you can see ghosts in the Penumbra. In others it is equally adamant that the Shadowlands can only be visited by special and dangerous Entropy magic.<br /> <br /> There's a few ways I can think of to reconcile these two that work... kind of, but it really depends on how hard you want interacting with ghosts to be. Unless you want ghosts to be significantly harder to work with than spirits, though, I'd just treat the Shadowlands as part of the Penumbra and let them see and interact with ghosts there. Then you only have to get into the complicated Underworld travel rules if your players really want to go to the Tempest or deeper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T11:45:55-07:00","id":1564545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564534#post1564534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cosmology is a problem but that I can kinda simplify without much effort!<br /> <br /> Thank you for helping tough</div> </div> </div> </div>Cosmology in Mage has three big problems.<br /> <br /> 1. It uses overly complicated language,<br /> <br /> 2. It is inconsistent,<br /> <br /> 3. It is referential to other WoD games.<br /> <br /> Both are partially deliberate, but end up being mostly confusing. In the end it's more useful to start from a baseline just as complete, but with simpler explanations and simplified systems you can complicate later, as you learn more.<br /> <br /> So the layers are more or less like this, with marks where you have to decide things. Don't worry too much about the decisions:<br /> <br /> 1. The Gauntlet. Just a barrier. It's the same for everything and has a rating that varies by local.<br /> <br /> 2. Quasi-Earths. When you cross the Gauntlet without Correspondence you usually have to go to one of those, defined by the Magic. Realms marked as Penumbrae may be the same, your choice:<br /> <br /> 2a. Astral Penumbra, maps perfectly to Earth and is its idealized version, shaped by emotion, beliefs and symbols. Has natural connections to the Astral Reaches (Level 3). Probably it's one of the Penumbrae.<br /> <br /> 2b. Spirit Penumbra, maps perfectly to Earth and is where its vitality sits, shaped by things and landscape on Earth, but empowered by &quot;importance&quot; (probably emotions, beliefs and symbols, but embodied in the thing they're linked to). Has natural connections to the Spirit Wilds (Level 3). Probably it's one of the Penumbrae.<br /> <br /> 2c. Low Penumbra, maps perfectly to Earth and is a decayed reflection, whatever you decide it means, empowered by whatever, maybe by memory of things gone. May have natural connections to the Shadowlands (Level 2), the Underworld (Level 3) or nothing, choose. Probably it's one of the Penumbrae.<br /> <br /> 2d. The Shadowlands, maps perfectly to Earth and is a decayed reflection, whatever you decide it means, empowered by memory of things gone. Has natural connections to the Underworld (Level 3). May be the same thing as the Low Penumbra. Probably it's one of the Penumbrae. COMES FROM WRAITH AND IS OPTIONAL.<br /> <br /> 2e. Chimeric Reality, maps perfectly to Earth and is a psychedelic trip made real, empowered by wonder and creativity. Has natural connections to the Near Dreaming (Level 3). May be one of the Penumbrae, or may be on Earth directly, or may be on the Dream Zone (Level 3/4).COMES FROM CHANGELING AND IS OPTIONAL.<br /> <br /> 2f. Everett Volumes. Those are NOT Penumbrae. They're alternative Earths. Usually they are other timelines, but may be stranger and have different rules of reality. They may be &quot;Level 0&quot; like Earth or stay Level 2, your choice. It's unclear if Material worlds too extremely different, like fantasy settings, exist here, your choice.<br /> <br /> 3. Otherworldly Expanses. Those places are unmoored from Earth completely and work like infinite hubs: their only commonality is that you can reach them from a Level 2 place:<br /> <br /> 3a. Astral Reaches, the Realms of Ideas. Has its own mind-based rules for some things and the place you arrive is an infinite extension of incongruous environments called the Vulgate. Think of places here like The Idea of a City, or the Toon Frontier: they're symbolic, but not terribly abstract, not specific and not important.<br /> <br /> 3b. Spirit Wilds, the Realm of Spirits. Yes, the game will make you use the word &quot;spirit&quot; to 3 or 4 different things. It's an infinite sequence of normal environments, but more grandiose. It has no other relevant name.<br /> <br /> 3c. Underworld, the Realm of Memory. Yes, of Memory. All destroyed things that are still remembered come here. They're not Ghosts, and they may not remain intact for long. If you are lucky or smart you'll arrive at a place called a Kingdom where the dead of a given area or something managed to establish protection against The Tempest. If not, you arrive at the Tempest and will start to get badly hurt, maybe die, become a Ghost, and be shredded again. COMES FROM WRAITH AND IS OPTIONAL, KINDA<br /> <br /> 3d. The Dreaming, Realm of Glamour. This is an infinite expanse of stories. Most of the place is wilderness, but may house anything. Here lives fairies, and they're weird. It has Paths where travel is safe-ish, and you risk not remembering shit if your trip when leaving it if you don't protect your mind enough.<br /> <br /> 4. Realms and Zones, the &quot;final destinations&quot;. Those are other realities in any sense, usually limited in size, but can be gigantic, even bigger than Earth.<br /> - Realms: you arrive at them from a Level 3 expanse. The Spires of the Astral Reaches have passages to Realms, the Spirit Wilds have paths to Realms. In the Underworld and the Dreaming this is usually deeper parts of the place, like the Labyrinth, but you can put Realms there, too.<br /> - Zones: just like Realms, but they extend their entrances to anywhere, including sometimes Earth. You're on your merry way and suddenly you see a strange door, big hollow tree, or any other thing that isn't very normal where you are, and if you enter you're in a Zone. The good side is that if you understand the rules of the Zone it isn't usually hard to leave. The Dream Zone has all dreams of everything that dreams, the Web is a reflection of the current Internet, both are reasonably easy to reach directly and leave safely.<br /> <br /> 5. The Near Horizon. It's like a tougher Gauntlet that separates all those things from Near Space. It is actually VISIBLE for everyone, but invisible just in the sense that it is colorless and transparent. Stars and planets actually shine through it, and Horizon Realms can be visible here too sometimes. IIRC it currently sits a little beyond the Moon.<br /> <br /> 6. Near Space. For Mages this is the best definition of &quot;where space begins&quot;. Few but significant Realms exist here, like the Shard Realms that may or may not be the source of Magic. This is prime Real Estate for artificial Realms, so you'll find most of them here, the Horizon Realms.<br /> <br /> 7. Far Horizon. This is a Gauntlet so tough it requires Spirit 5 to even try to cross. There Lies Monsters. Reality as we know it has no meaning\u200b beyond this threshold, yet all other stars lie there. If anything isn't accessible from the other Umbrae, it is from here, but it's incredibly dangerous. Aliens do come from there too, they're an actual, real threat. Do what you want from here on, only one Realm was ever built and/or visited this far, and it is now lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T12:00:02-07:00","id":1564546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564545#post1564545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cosmology in Mage has three big problems.<br /> <br /> 1. It uses overly complicated language,<br /> <br /> 2. It is inconsistent,<br /> <br /> 3. It is referential to other WoD games.<br /> <br /> Both are partially deliberate, but end up being mostly confusing. In the end it's more useful to start from a baseline just as complete, but with simpler explanations and simplified systems you can complicate later, as you learn more.<br /> <br /> So the layers are more or less like this, with marks where you have to decide things. Don't worry too much about the decisions:<br /> <br /> 1. The Gauntlet. Just a barrier. It's the same for everything and has a rating that varies by local.<br /> <br /> 2. Quasi-Earths. When you cross the Gauntlet without Correspondence you usually have to go to one of those, defined by the Magic. Realms marked as Penumbrae may be the same, your choice:<br /> <br /> 2a. Astral Penumbra, maps perfectly to Earth and is its idealized version, shaped by emotion, beliefs and symbols. Has natural connections to the Astral Reaches (Level 3). Probably it's one of the Penumbrae.<br /> <br /> 2b. Spirit Penumbra, maps perfectly to Earth and is where its vitality sits, shaped by things and landscape on Earth, but empowered by &quot;importance&quot; (probably emotions, beliefs and symbols, but embodied in the thing they're linked to). Has natural connections to the Spirit Wilds (Level 3). Probably it's one of the Penumbrae.<br /> <br /> 2c. Low Penumbra, maps perfectly to Earth and is a decayed reflection, whatever you decide it means, empowered by whatever, maybe by memory of things gone. May have natural connections to the Shadowlands (Level 2), the Underworld (Level 3) or nothing, choose. Probably it's one of the Penumbrae.<br /> <br /> 2d. The Shadowlands, maps perfectly to Earth and is a decayed reflection, whatever you decide it means, empowered by memory of things gone. Has natural connections to the Underworld (Level 3). May be the same thing as the Low Penumbra. Probably it's one of the Penumbrae. COMES FROM WRAITH AND IS OPTIONAL.<br /> <br /> 2e. Chimeric Reality, maps perfectly to Earth and is a psychedelic trip made real, empowered by wonder and creativity. Has natural connections to the Near Dreaming (Level 3). May be one of the Penumbrae, or may be on Earth directly, or may be on the Dream Zone (Level 3/4).COMES FROM CHANGELING AND IS OPTIONAL.<br /> <br /> 2f. Everett Volumes. Those are NOT Penumbrae. They're alternative Earths. Usually they are other timelines, but may be stranger and have different rules of reality. They may be &quot;Level 0&quot; like Earth or stay Level 2, your choice. It's unclear if Material worlds too extremely different, like fantasy settings, exist here, your choice.<br /> <br /> 3. Otherworldly Expanses. Those places are unmoored from Earth completely and work like infinite hubs: their only commonality is that you can reach them from a Level 2 place:<br /> <br /> 3a. Astral Reaches, the Realms of Ideas. Has its own mind-based rules for some things and the place you arrive is an infinite extension of incongruous environments called the Vulgate. Think of places here like The Idea of a City, or the Toon Frontier: they're symbolic, but not terribly abstract, not specific and not important.<br /> <br /> 3b. Spirit Wilds, the Realm of Spirits. Yes, the game will make you use the word &quot;spirit&quot; to 3 or 4 different things. It's an infinite sequence of normal environments, but more grandiose. It has no other relevant name.<br /> <br /> 3c. Underworld, the Realm of Memory. Yes, of Memory. All destroyed things that are still remembered come here. They're not Ghosts, and they may not remain intact for long. If you are lucky or smart you'll arrive at a place called a Kingdom where the dead of a given area or something managed to establish protection against The Tempest. If not, you arrive at the Tempest and will start to get badly hurt, maybe die, become a Ghost, and be shredded again. COMES FROM WRAITH AND IS OPTIONAL, KINDA<br /> <br /> 3d. The Dreaming, Realm of Glamour. This is an infinite expanse of stories. Most of the place is wilderness, but may house anything. Here lives fairies, and they're weird. It has Paths where travel is safe-ish, and you risk not remembering shit if your trip when leaving it if you don't protect your mind enough.<br /> <br /> 4. Realms and Zones, the &quot;final destinations&quot;. Those are other realities in any sense, usually limited in size, but can be gigantic, even bigger than Earth.<br /> - Realms: you arrive at them from a Level 3 expanse. The Spires of the Astral Reaches have passages to Realms, the Spirit Wilds have paths to Realms. In the Underworld and the Dreaming this is usually deeper parts of the place, like the Labyrinth, but you can put Realms there, too.<br /> - Zones: just like Realms, but they extend their entrances to anywhere, including sometimes Earth. You're on your merry way and suddenly you see a strange door, big hollow tree, or any other thing that isn't very normal where you are, and if you enter you're in a Zone. The good side is that if you understand the rules of the Zone it isn't usually hard to leave. The Dream Zone has all dreams of everything that dreams, the Web is a reflection of the current Internet, both are reasonably easy to reach directly and leave safely.<br /> <br /> 5. The Near Horizon. It's like a tougher Gauntlet that separates all those things from Near Space. It is actually VISIBLE for everyone, but invisible just in the sense that it is colorless and transparent. Stars and planets actually shine through it, and Horizon Realms can be visible here too sometimes. IIRC it currently sits a little beyond the Moon.<br /> <br /> 6. Near Space. For Mages this is the best definition of &quot;where space begins&quot;. Few but significant Realms exist here, like the Shard Realms that may or may not be the source of Magic. This is prime Real Estate for artificial Realms, so you'll find most of them here, the Horizon Realms.<br /> <br /> 7. Far Horizon. This is a Gauntlet so tough it requires Spirit 5 to even try to cross. There Lies Monsters. Reality as we know it has no meaning beyond this threshold, yet all other stars lie there. If anything isn't accessible from the other Umbrae, it is from here, but it's incredibly dangerous. Aliens do come from there too, they're an actual, real threat. Do what you want from here on, only one Realm was ever built and/or visited this far, and it is now lost.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is really a lot to take in and map; what do you think the implications could be if I simplified it a bit? It's A LOT, I am not sure I can even understand it properly. And we ahven't even mentioned Heaven and Hell and that mounain or tree that connects everything (maybe)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","user":"~Ozz~","date":". 10-05-2026, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T12:01:47-07:00","id":1564547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564538#post1564538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You aren't alone. Mage is really a mess on this point. In some places it is really clear that the Shadowlands <b>are</b> the Penumbra (as seen through the Vidare Mortem) and even goes so far as to say you can see ghosts in the Penumbra. In others it is equally adamant that the Shadowlands can only be visited by special and dangerous Entropy magic.<br /> <br /> There's a few ways I can think of to reconcile these two that work... kind of, but it really depends on how hard you want interacting with ghosts to be. Unless you want ghosts to be significantly harder to work with than spirits, though, I'd just treat the Shadowlands as part of the Penumbra and let them see and interact with ghosts there. Then you only have to get into the complicated Underworld travel rules if your players really want to go to the Tempest or deeper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You can bet I will go with the simplest way possible, I dont want my adventure to focus heavily on the Umbrae, I want my players mostly on hearth if possible. I Just wanna give them the chance to use the spirit sphere properly but they dont need all that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T13:54:15-07:00","id":1564551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564546#post1564546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really a lot to take in and map; what do you think the implications could be if I simplified it a bit? It's A LOT, I am not sure I can even understand it properly. And we ahven't even mentioned Heaven and Hell and that mounain or tree that connects everything (maybe)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's simpler than it seems, just follow the numbers and study only one thing at a time. Anything you don't need at the moment just ignore, w<br /> <br /> Heaven and Hell are Realms. Anything you think off as another reality in the usual sense is a Realm. Sometimes multiple Realms that have the same name because they're different versions of the same thing.<br /> <br /> So you find them in the Astral Reaches, in the Spires.<br /> <br /> You can simplify a lot, but I'd recommend just ignore bits until they matter.<br /> <br /> Let's try the <u><b>Minimum Viable Umbra</b></u>, just in case your players want to go there:<br /> <br /> 1. Gauntlet<br /> <br /> 2. Penumbrae. Keep 3 and keep them separate, that increases size but simplify use:<br /> <br /> 2a. Astral Penumbra<br /> 2b. Spirit Penumbra<br /> 2c. Shadowlands<br /> <br /> 3. Expanses. They have some places to wander and also contain Realms:<br /> <br /> 3a. Astral Reaches<br /> 3b. Spirit Wilds<br /> 3c. Underworld<br /> <br /> 4. Realms and Zones. Everything, basically.<br /> <br /> Hell, Heaven, Hades, Arcadia, Pangaea, Abyss, anything at all is a Realm. Choose if it is in the Astral Reaches, the Spirit Wilds, or it is a Zone.<br /> <br /> Zones are just Realms that have connections everywhere.<br /> - Dream Zone (Reaches anything that dreams),<br /> - Digital Web (Touches every computer with a connection),<br /> - Aelder Bole (The giant tree, has passages everywhere),<br /> - Mirror Zone (Connects all mirrors).<br /> <br /> So the map is:<br /> <br /> Gauntlet<br /> |<br /> |&gt; Astral Penumbra &gt; Astral Reaches &gt; Realms<br /> |&gt; Spirit Penumbra &gt; Spirit Wilds &gt; Realms<br /> |&gt; Shadowlands &gt; Underworld &gt; The Labyrinth<br /> |&gt; Everett Volumes (any alternate Earth)<br /> <br /> Zones are outside the map.<br /> <br /> And that's it. Everything else is optional complications you can explore later. And every world you can conceive is just a Realm.<br /> <br /> What a Realm/Zone is? Whatever you want, if you want to define at all. The map isn't about what anywhere means, just how to get there.<br /> <br /> Horizon is for space. Everything above is Earth-like and you only have to travel with Spirit. For anything related to Horizon you also have to fly somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T00:56:55-07:00","id":1564555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564538#post1564538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren't alone. Mage is really a mess on this point. In some places it is really clear that the Shadowlands <b>are</b> the Penumbra (as seen through the Vidare Mortem) and even goes so far as to say you can see ghosts in the Penumbra. In others it is equally adamant that the Shadowlands can only be visited by special and dangerous Entropy magic.<br /> <br /> There's a few ways I can think of to reconcile these two that work... kind of, but it really depends on how hard you want interacting with ghosts to be. Unless you want ghosts to be significantly harder to work with than spirits, though, I'd just treat the Shadowlands as part of the Penumbra and let them see and interact with ghosts there. Then you only have to get into the complicated Underworld travel rules if your players really want to go to the Tempest or deeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I interpret the Shadowlands is that there's the Dark Penumbra, and then there's the &quot;Shadowlands proper&quot;.<br /> <br /> The former is where the Tempest and Wraith Society is. The &quot;deeper&quot; parts of the underworld, basically, that you &quot;descend into&quot;. Wraiths go there to have adventures and get involved in Ghost Politics.<br /> <br /> The latter is the parts nearest the Skinlands, and thus most resembles it. From what I understand as someone with very little WtO knowledge, Wraiths can only hang out here nearby to objects or locations important to them in life (their Fetters). They typically &quot;go topside&quot; for a variety of reasons. To watch over their loved ones/descendants. To contact spirit mediums. To guard their Fetters. To gather Pathos. To torment the new owners into leaving their house. To investigate their death. To avoid Ghost Politics. To avoid the Tempest. To avoid getting turned into ashtrays. Etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Under this model, a Mage game involving the Spirit sphere will include ghosts only in those places where it makes narrative sense, and then not all the time. A school might have a kid bullied to a permanent end hanging around. Hospitals might have an elderly person who spent years there, either continuously or on and off. A house might be haunted by its former owner(s), obvs. The home of a spirit medium might have the ghosts of people whose Fetters the medium holds for safekeeping. A street corner might have a ghost of one who got run over or mugged to a permanent end. Etc, etc.<br /> <br /> And, of course, a murder scene MIGHT have the ghost of the victim (or another ghost who saw what happened). The victim's ghost might still be in their new-ghost &quot;cocoon&quot;, and thus unable to talk. Though this might, itself, be a quest; figuring out how to either free them, or get another Wraith there to wake them in their place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T07:49:54-07:00","id":1564561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564555#post1564555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I interpret the Shadowlands is that there's the Dark Penumbra, and then there's the &quot;Shadowlands proper&quot;.<br /> <br /> The former is where the Tempest and Wraith Society is. The &quot;deeper&quot; parts of the underworld, basically, that you &quot;descend into&quot;. Wraiths go there to have adventures and get involved in Ghost Politics.<br /> <br /> The latter is the parts nearest the Skinlands, and thus most resembles it. From what I understand as someone with very little WtO knowledge, Wraiths can only hang out here nearby to objects or locations important to them in life (their Fetters). They typically &quot;go topside&quot; for a variety of reasons. To watch over their loved ones/descendants. To contact spirit mediums. To guard their Fetters. To gather Pathos. To torment the new owners into leaving their house. To investigate their death. To avoid Ghost Politics. To avoid the Tempest. To avoid getting turned into ashtrays. Etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Under this model, a Mage game involving the Spirit sphere will include ghosts only in those places where it makes narrative sense, and then not all the time. A school might have a kid bullied to a permanent end hanging around. Hospitals might have an elderly person who spent years there, either continuously or on and off. A house might be haunted by its former owner(s), obvs. The home of a spirit medium might have the ghosts of people whose Fetters the medium holds for safekeeping. A street corner might have a ghost of one who got run over or mugged to a permanent end. Etc, etc.<br /> <br /> And, of course, a murder scene MIGHT have the ghost of the victim (or another ghost who saw what happened). The victim's ghost might still be in their new-ghost &quot;cocoon&quot;, and thus unable to talk. Though this might, itself, be a quest; figuring out how to either free them, or get another Wraith there to wake them in their place.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good and usable system for a typical Mage game. It provides reasonable access to ghosts while keeping the scope limited. It encourages mages to do legwork if they want to find a specific ghost. It makes every ghost and every haunt a potential story hook. It does deviate from Wraith mechanically, but it brings about the same situation Wraith is trying to, at least from the side of the living. It wouldn't work for an actual crossover game, but for Mage its a quick and easy shortcut. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I understand as someone with very little WtO knowledge, Wraiths can only hang out here nearby to objects or locations important to them in life (their Fetters). </div> </div> </div>Wraiths can actually visit the Shadowlands version of any part of the Skinlands and, if they have the right powers, interact with any part of the Skinlands. However, for statistical, metaphysical, and political reasons they are far more likely to interact with places that are either very important to them or are associated with death and where they won't be seen doing so by most other ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T09:11:41-07:00","id":1564563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564555#post1564555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">include ghosts only in those places where it makes narrative sense, and then not all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question with ghosts is defining how much that is, because this tell something about your view of the <b><i>cause</i></b> of ghosts in the setting, how common they are. Or, out another way, how haunted the world is. This is narrative sense, and is world building.<br /> <br /> It takes unfinished business to form a ghost. But how many humans finish their business still alive in the World of Darkness? How many people die every year?<br /> <br /> Now, in real life, or best estimates are the total human population that ever lived is between 115 and 120 billion. It means the dead population is ~110 billion in the real world, and today 60+ million die every year. If 1/10 leave ghosts and 1/10 ghosts stay in the Penumbra, that's 600 thousands fresh ghosts every year.<br /> <br /> How much is that in the setting? How many people the world secretly has in excess, how many die every year? How many leave ghosts because of all the possible reasons someone living in the World of Darkness may have? How many of those stay close to the Skinlands in a regular basis?<br /> <br /> Your ghost population isn't just background, it is a statement. And you don't need all of them to be powerful as spirits, let most be weak and with no particular way to affect Earth and you can have as many as you want.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can as much want few of them. To stress how high the bar is, or unpredictable the process, or how many are prevented to stay on Earth for whatever reason (including but not necessarily the same as those in Wraith).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T10:42:59-07:00","id":1564567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564551#post1564551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's simpler than it seems, just follow the numbers and study only one thing at a time. Anything you don't need at the moment just ignore, w<br /> <br /> Heaven and Hell are Realms. Anything you think off as another reality in the usual sense is a Realm. Sometimes multiple Realms that have the same name because they're different versions of the same thing.<br /> <br /> So you find them in the Astral Reaches, in the Spires.<br /> <br /> You can simplify a lot, but I'd recommend just ignore bits until they matter.<br /> <br /> Let's try the <u><b>Minimum Viable Umbra</b></u>, just in case your players want to go there:<br /> <br /> 1. Gauntlet<br /> <br /> 2. Penumbrae. Keep 3 and keep them separate, that increases size but simplify use:<br /> <br /> 2a. Astral Penumbra<br /> 2b. Spirit Penumbra<br /> 2c. Shadowlands<br /> <br /> 3. Expanses. They have some places to wander and also contain Realms:<br /> <br /> 3a. Astral Reaches<br /> 3b. Spirit Wilds<br /> 3c. Underworld<br /> <br /> 4. Realms and Zones. Everything, basically.<br /> <br /> Hell, Heaven, Hades, Arcadia, Pangaea, Abyss, anything at all is a Realm. Choose if it is in the Astral Reaches, the Spirit Wilds, or it is a Zone.<br /> <br /> Zones are just Realms that have connections everywhere.<br /> - Dream Zone (Reaches anything that dreams),<br /> - Digital Web (Touches every computer with a connection),<br /> - Aelder Bole (The giant tree, has passages everywhere),<br /> - Mirror Zone (Connects all mirrors).<br /> <br /> So the map is:<br /> <br /> Gauntlet<br /> |<br /> |&gt; Astral Penumbra &gt; Astral Reaches &gt; Realms<br /> |&gt; Spirit Penumbra &gt; Spirit Wilds &gt; Realms<br /> |&gt; Shadowlands &gt; Underworld &gt; The Labyrinth<br /> |&gt; Everett Volumes (any alternate Earth)<br /> <br /> Zones are outside the map.<br /> <br /> And that's it. Everything else is optional complications you can explore later. And every world you can conceive is just a Realm.<br /> <br /> What a Realm/Zone is? Whatever you want, if you want to define at all. The map isn't about what anywhere means, just how to get there.<br /> <br /> Horizon is for space. Everything above is Earth-like and you only have to travel with Spirit. For anything related to Horizon you also have to fly somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's still too much for my poor brain, I'm gonna go with simple and grounded with most of the stuff I am not sure how to handle just being a realm. It could work right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T11:14:19-07:00","id":1564568,"title":"","content":"Rather than that, I would suggest to roll with the punches. You may find that while the whole cosmology it's very large and daunting, most mages will only interact with a tiny fragment of it.<br /> <br /> I.E: Virtual Adepts and computer-curious mages care about the Digital Web, but very few others do - so if one doesn't have those one likely doesn't need to pay much heed to it.<br /> <br /> *Focus on the Penumbrae, because that's the part of the Umbra they're going to interact for sure, then expand outwards.<br /> <br /> *A good idea to buld outwards could be to focus on the Beliefs of your players. These not only colour their interactions, but also inform you what interactions they <i>want </i>to have<br /> <br /> For instance: Let's say a mage believes in ancestor worship. Then you need spirits that represent their ancestors (could be ghosts), and these likely don't live on the Penumbra (unless he has a haunted house or something) - so you need an afterlife (that's a Realm) complete with whatever entities should reside on it (gods, heavenly envoys, whatever...)<br /> <br /> Now, where is this place on the map? - I would suggest to see what kind of magick the mage does, because this is what they will use to connect with them.<br /> <br /> We could debate if such a realm should be on the Underworld, where ghosts live. On the High Umbra, where gods live. I would <i>err</i> towards <i>both</i> ussing Helheim as an example (Hella's realm exists on both the Astral Umbra and the Underworld - these are conected and can be used to travel betwen worlds - but, realy, even nordic mages are unlikely to know enough to actually exploit this feature) - but it's less likely to impact play. Far better to focus on your players, and if that means you end with Ghosts on the Middle Umbra, well, just say the Realm has connections to the Underworld and that's that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-06-2026, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T13:17:05-07:00","id":1564571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564567#post1564567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's still too much for my poor brain, I'm gonna go with simple and grounded with most of the stuff I am not sure how to handle just being a realm. It could work right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically what Aleph said.<br /> <br /> Focus on this:<br /> <br /> Gauntlet -&gt; Penumbra -&gt; Realms<br /> <br /> Then ask what the PCs think of other worlds.<br /> <br /> Your goal is to make what they think, possible.<br /> <br /> No less, no more.<br /> <br /> If a player wants animist spirits, their Magic access animist spirits.<br /> <br /> If a player wants the courts of the gods, their Magic access the courts of the gods<br /> <br /> If a player wants ghosts, their Magic access ghosts.<br /> <br /> If a player wants alternate realities, their Magic access alternate realities.<br /> <br /> If a player does not want something in their Paradigm, their Magic can't go there without help, so it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> If a player wants something stranger, give them what they want and come ask if you need help.<br /> <br /> If a player wants to know what exists between Realms or in space, only then you need a little extra.<br /> <br /> Crucially: <u><b>don't overthink</b></u>.<br /> <br /> Forget the book. Its greatest problem is that it thinks too much. The book doesn't help, and if you try to reconcile what we say with the book before understanding, it will only get in the way.<br /> <br /> We've all been where you are now, and the most experienced ones got it with time and too much effort to disentangle things. And our big frustration is exactly that: the book doesn't help whatsoever. What we found in the end was a system considerably simpler than the constant highly abstract metaphysical spiel in the book makes it appear.<br /> <br /> <b>And making the stuff you don't know how to handle into a Realm is actually the point</b>.<br /> <br /> That's it in a nutshell.<br /> <br /> Only 5 things are not Realms:<br /> 1. Earth,<br /> 2. Penumbra,<br /> 3. Astral Reaches,<br /> 4. Spirit Wilds,<br /> 5. Underworld.<br /> <br /> From those, you only have to understand the Earth (obviously) and Penumbra. The other 3 are in a need-to-know basis.<br /> <br /> How you reach a given Realm?<br /> However makes sense.<br /> <br /> Learning more of the cosmology make things easier to navigate, but isn't necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T08:15:46-07:00","id":1564585,"title":"","content":"Okay, I will take this approach; the player with spirit is a Wicca, so I guess my focus should be the middle umbra and nature related stuff. I will worry about the digital web when the tech PC will get points in spirit. I will still make it simple as monteparnas is suggesting. I will not bother with mount quaf or stuff like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T09:17:43-07:00","id":1564586,"title":"","content":"As a heads up, there are ways of accessing the digital web that don't use Spirit. Does your tech PC have Correspondence 2?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T11:52:18-07:00","id":1564590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564586#post1564586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a heads up, there are ways of accessing the digital web that don't use Spirit. Does your tech PC have Correspondence 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... 3 points in correspondence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T16:03:42-07:00","id":1564596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564585#post1564585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I will take this approach; the player with spirit is a Wicca, so I guess my focus should be the middle umbra and nature related stuff. I will worry about the digital web when the tech PC will get points in spirit. I will still make it simple as monteparnas is suggesting. I will not bother with mount quaf or stuff like that</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect. For the Middle Umbra/Spirit Wilds you can also look <i>Werewolf the Apocalypse</i>. It isn't a 1:1 translation, but will be tens of times more helpful.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><i>Middle Umbra / Spirit Realms</i></b></span><br /> <br /> Still the basic is: <i>looks like Earth, but <b>grandiose and intense</b></i>. Nature is intense, industrialization is intense, pollution and decay are intense, but most things are recognizable. In Werewolf cities have way more Pattern Spiders than in Mage, so you only need the &quot;<u><i><b>same but bigger than life</b></i></u>&quot; part.<br /> <br /> It's not a representation of the Earth, either, so you just <b><u>make up geography as you go</u></b>. There are some people that use it for shortcuts for this reason. <u><b>Add spirits and myth</b></u> shenanigans like roads made of stardust that go up to the sky or whatever.<br /> <br /> You'll find all sorts of <u>spirits wandering around and it is legitimately dangerous</u>, but is not a lot, <u>just more than the Penumbra</u>. <u>Most spirits will be on Realms</u>. The place is full of passages back to the Penumbra and to Realms aplenty, they look anyway you want them to.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Beware floating roads made of Moon light</b></i>. The <b>Werewolves</b> build and use them, and won't accept intruders. They almost always link two Nature Nodes back on Earth under Werewolf control, so they may serve as a marker of areas close to the Earth, but <b><u><i>werewolves don't accept even their fondest allies and family</i></u></b> near the actual Nodes and you'll generally find one or <b>two dozen</b> of them in one at any given time.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><i>The Digital Web / Network Zone</i></b></span><br /> <br /> The Digital Web can be accessed from <i><b>any computer with a connection, anywhere in the multiverse</b></i>. Easier with Spirit, but many groups know the secret to do it with Correspondence. A connection to the internet is ideal, but in a pinch you can brute force on any two linked computers.<br /> <br /> Picture an illustrative representation of a data grid. The place is that made literal. Any SciFi movie or comic about navigating the web itself will work as reference. Player Number One not, just because it is a Second Life style instead, it is better for Nodes in the Web.<br /> <br /> And that's it. <b>Links and Nodes</b>. From outside they look like giant connected structures of whatever material you want, and at least the size of a Metro tunnel. From inside <i><b>Links are whatever transport system</b></i> you can imagine. <i><b>Nodes are specific computers</b></i> or processing units turned into metaphor. Metaphor you can touch, drink, fuck, etc. Good references if you need are <i>Tron</i> and <i>Reboot</i>, since they're classic and won't add noise.<br /> <br /> Mostly tech Mages use it to meet and chat, so it's just a big, weird tavern, but you can affect a computer from its analogous Node, or block a signal by blocking the Link in the Digital Web. It is a thing to use the Digital Web to bypass safe systems too tough to take with mundane hack.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><i>Zones in General</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <i><b>Zones are your toys</b></i>. Use them if and when you want unless a player decides to go there specifically. <i><b>They're not there to understand, they're there for <u>Deus Ex Machina</u></b></i>. You can put a natural passage to a Zone wherever you want and the exit wherever else. Again, <i><b>anywhere in the Multiverse</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Use, toy, scrap. If they want to go back, they go figure out how that works. Other than that, your only obligation is to be consistent on what a natural passage to a particular Zone looks like.<br /> <br /> <i><b>This is the secret: you don't have to understand</b></i> them. In fact, no one understands them. The book is so arcane about them precisely 'cause it's saying in extremely purple prose that &quot;no one has the slightest idea&quot;. They're just there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T02:40:02-07:00","id":1564602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564596#post1564596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perfect. For the Middle Umbra/Spirit Wilds you can also look <i>Werewolf the Apocalypse</i>. It isn't a 1:1 translation, but will be tens of times more helpful.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><i>Middle Umbra / Spirit Realms</i></b></span><br /> <br /> Still the basic is: <i>looks like Earth, but <b>grandiose and intense</b></i>. Nature is intense, industrialization is intense, pollution and decay are intense, but most things are recognizable. In Werewolf cities have way more Pattern Spiders than in Mage, so you only need the &quot;<u><i><b>same but bigger than life</b></i></u>&quot; part.<br /> <br /> It's not a representation of the Earth, either, so you just <b><u>make up geography as you go</u></b>. There are some people that use it for shortcuts for this reason. <u><b>Add spirits and myth</b></u> shenanigans like roads made of stardust that go up to the sky or whatever.<br /> <br /> You'll find all sorts of <u>spirits wandering around and it is legitimately dangerous</u>, but is not a lot, <u>just more than the Penumbra</u>. <u>Most spirits will be on Realms</u>. The place is full of passages back to the Penumbra and to Realms aplenty, they look anyway you want them to.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Beware floating roads made of Moon light</b></i>. The <b>Werewolves</b> build and use them, and won't accept intruders. They almost always link two Nature Nodes back on Earth under Werewolf control, so they may serve as a marker of areas close to the Earth, but <b><u><i>werewolves don't accept even their fondest allies and family</i></u></b> near the actual Nodes and you'll generally find one or <b>two dozen</b> of them in one at any given time.</div> </div> </div> </div>This look absolutely doable! Thank you so much! I am guessing in Middle Umbra portals would be toward &quot;thematic zones&quot; right? I.E a portal toward a fire realm and not one toward the digital web.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564596#post1564596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><i>The Digital Web / Network Zone</i></b></span><br /> <br /> The Digital Web can be accessed from <i><b>any computer with a connection, anywhere in the multiverse</b></i>. Easier with Spirit, but many groups know the secret to do it with Correspondence. A connection to the internet is ideal, but in a pinch you can brute force on any two linked computers.<br /> <br /> Picture an illustrative representation of a data grid. The place is that made literal. Any SciFi movie or comic about navigating the web itself will work as reference. Player Number One not, just because it is a Second Life style instead, it is better for Nodes in the Web.<br /> <br /> And that's it. <b>Links and Nodes</b>. From outside they look like giant connected structures of whatever material you want, and at least the size of a Metro tunnel. From inside <i><b>Links are whatever transport system</b></i> you can imagine. <i><b>Nodes are specific computers</b></i> or processing units turned into metaphor. Metaphor you can touch, drink, fuck, etc. Good references if you need are <i>Tron</i> and <i>Reboot</i>, since they're classic and won't add noise.<br /> <br /> Mostly tech Mages use it to meet and chat, so it's just a big, weird tavern, but you can affect a computer from its analogous Node, or block a signal by blocking the Link in the Digital Web. It is a thing to use the Digital Web to bypass safe systems too tough to take with mundane hack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay this feels simple enough, I will find a way to visualize it and properly describe it, but it's a problem farin the future; my tech guy has correspondence 3, but they are orphans so no access at the moment to &quot;secret methods&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564596#post1564596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><i>Zones in General</i></b></span><br /> <br /> <i><b>Zones are your toys</b></i>. Use them if and when you want unless a player decides to go there specifically. <i><b>They're not there to understand, they're there for <u>Deus Ex Machina</u></b></i>. You can put a natural passage to a Zone wherever you want and the exit wherever else. Again, <i><b>anywhere in the Multiverse</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Use, toy, scrap. If they want to go back, they go figure out how that works. Other than that, your only obligation is to be consistent on what a natural passage to a particular Zone looks like.<br /> <br /> <i><b>This is the secret: you don't have to understand</b></i> them. In fact, no one understands them. The book is so arcane about them precisely 'cause it's saying in extremely purple prose that &quot;no one has the slightest idea&quot;. They're just there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the part I am most excited about tbh!! I can go wild and give my players some weird experiences as a &quot;break&quot; from the more grounded &quot;orphans figuring shit out&quot; style<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T20:00:17-07:00","id":1564627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564602#post1564602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This look absolutely doable! Thank you so much! I am guessing in Middle Umbra portals would be toward &quot;thematic zones&quot; right? I.E a portal toward a fire realm and not one toward the digital web.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be whatever, even because it can have any kind of realistic environment, not just natural ones. So you definitely have portals to thematic realms, but also to most realms you may need a portal to.<br /> <br /> Remember: it is also the Umbra of cities, server farms, nuclear powerplants, toxic waste dumps and anything that has a physical representation in the world.<br /> <br /> So do you want a passage to Hades or Sheol? Since those places are defined by caves, they have passages in the Middle Umbra. Olympus probably has one, accessible through a path that start in the Penumbra of the actual Mount Olympus in Greece.<br /> <br /> If any realm seems close enough to something that physically exists in the world, it may have a passage in the Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> On the Digital Web: first, if a character carries a computer with them, and today a smartphone counts, they have a possible link to the Digital Web.<br /> <br /> Also, <i><b>having passages everywhere is a trait of the Digital Web</b></i>. In the Middle Umbra they may look like giant roots, spider webs, anything that resembles branching lines or paths. You can look for a door inside the Link or just climb it until you're not in the Middle Umbra anymore.<br /> <br /> But apply what I said earlier: it is a Zone, it has passages if you want, where you want, for as long as you want, and you have no obligation to be consistent. Mapping natural passages to the Digital Web is a legitimate way of dealing with it if you want to play with that, but has no guarantees.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564602#post1564602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay this feels simple enough, I will find a way to visualize it and properly describe it, but it's a problem farin the future; my tech guy has correspondence 3, but they are orphans so no access at the moment to &quot;secret methods&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Good.<br /> <br /> Overall you can vary description if you want. A given Link or Node will almost always look the same, but different Links and Nodes can look however you want even if they're close.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>~Ozz~</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1564468-one-of-my-players-started-putting-points-into-spirit-help-me-out-with-the-rules?p=1564602#post1564602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the part I am most excited about tbh!! I can go wild and give my players some weird experiences as a &quot;break&quot; from the more grounded &quot;orphans figuring shit out&quot; style</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you got it!<br /> <br /> This is the thing about Zones that the book is absurdly obtuse to explain. They're just worlds that have passages anywhere the ST wants.<br /> <br /> So the section on them isn't a structure to follow. <b>It is a menu</b>.<br /> <br /> Pick whatever you want, when you want, put a passage where you want. They appear on Earth and the Penumbra, in the Expanses, any Realm and even within each other.<br /> <br /> Why? No one knows, so doesn't matter. They're unpredictable, which means you have control.<br /> <br /> If a player ever wants to seek one of them in particular, like is common with the Digital Web, let them figure it out while you go look that Zone up.<br /> <br /> Otherwise whatever you don't want to use yet they simply won't find passages, so it doesn't matter. The beauty of the Umbra when the book isn't overcomplicating things is that what you don't want or don't understand simply don't get in your way, it's safe to ignore with no need to rewrite anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T05:54:20-07:00","id":1564637,"title":"","content":"monteparnas, you are way better than the book! I feel I am ready, I feel like I got it! It will be fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29177-~ozz~","name":"~Ozz~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-12T01:18:53-07:00","id":1564701,"title":"","content":"Monteparnas's point about the rulebook being a &quot;menu&quot; is very apt. The rulebook (regardless of edition) is a toolbox. A collection of options all in one place (or, often, spread out over a bunch of supplements). Every item isn't FOR every ST/player. Each, rather, is the perfect tool for a particular ST/player.<br /> <br /> Most games will never have reason to use the Certaman rules. Hell, a lot of Order of Hermes games, or one involving OoH PCs, will never involve Certaman. And that's fine, because it's not FOR them. It's FOR the people who want highly ritualized magickal duels between Hermetic magi.<br /> <br /> The rulebook needs to get into the weeds of a LOT of topics, because it needs to be a resource for any kind of game the designers imagined (or at least that they considered likely to come up). It gets dense because LIFE is dense and complicated and philosophically varied. A game ABOUT that complexity and philosophical variance needs a lot of options.<br /> <br /> But that also means any given game mechanic or setting element is liable to only be relevant to a narrow slice of the playerbase. <i>And that's fine</i>.<br /> <br /> Shrink the scope of your creative effort to what's important to YOUR Chronicle, and everything else will fall into place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}